From bfed1ef4d205b21da086dfe8e5881f1b1a74c787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Suhaas Borra <mehersuhaas123@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:09:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ui/sdl2: add clipboard sharing via qemu-vdagent

Adds ui/sdl2-clipboard.c, a host-clipboard <-> qemu-vdagent bridge for
the SDL display, mirroring what ui/gtk-clipboard.c does for GTK (SDL
never got this upstream, see QEMU issue #471). Enables --enable-spice
in build.sh to compile the qemu-vdagent chardev backend; no -spice
display/network port is opened at runtime.

Verified end-to-end: qemu-vdagent capability handshake completes, the
clipboard-grab message reaches the guest, and xclip confirms both
directions work at the X11 layer. Native Wayland guest apps under
niri are not yet reached -- that gap is in spice-vdagent (X11-only
clipboard implementation) and xwayland-satellite (no X11-to-native-
Wayland clipboard bridge), not in this fork.
