+## Clipboard Sharing
+
+Add these flags to share the clipboard between host and guest:
+
+```bash
+qemu-system-x86_64.exe \
+  ... \
+  -device virtio-serial-pci \
+  -chardev qemu-vdagent,id=vdagent,name=vdagent,clipboard=on \
+  -device virtserialport,chardev=vdagent,id=vdagent,name=com.redhat.spice.0
+```
+
+In the guest, install `spice-vdagent` (stock Ubuntu package: `apt install spice-vdagent`). It runs as both a system service (`spice-vdagentd`) and a per-session user service (`spice-vdagent`), started automatically once installed.
+
+**Current scope**: clipboard sync works correctly for any X11 or XWayland application in the guest (verified both directions with `xclip`). It does **not** yet reach native Wayland applications under niri. Root cause is guest-side, not this fork: `spice-vdagent`'s clipboard implementation is X11-selection-only (`XConvertSelection`, no `wlr-data-control` support at all — confirmed via `strings` on the binary), and niri's XWayland provider (`xwayland-satellite`) does not bridge that X11 selection into niri's native Wayland clipboard the way GNOME's Mutter does internally for its own embedded Xwayland. Fixing this would mean patching `xwayland-satellite` or niri, not QEMU — out of scope for this repo.
+
 ## Syncing with Upstream
 
 This fork tracks [QEMU upstream](https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu). All custom changes are in a single commit on top of the upstream tag, so rebasing is straightforward:
